{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1525986-m20-and-kuei-jin","id":1525986,"title":"M20 and Kuei Jin","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-11-26T18:04:40-08:00","id":1525986,"title":"M20 and Kuei Jin","content":"Greetings,<br /> <br /> Based in a long standing game, some doubts regarding Kindred of the East arise:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Kuei-Jin can absorbe Quintessence when feeding, can mages use Yang, Yin and/or Demon Chi?</li> <li>If the answer to the previous question is YES, what levels of Prime and any other Sphere are needed?</li> <li>What levels and which Spheres are needed to dectect the P\u2019o Nature?</li> <li>What levels and which Spheres are needed to alter/interact/modify the P\u2019o?</li> <li>In Yomi Wan, what levels and which Spheres are needed to protect against the spiritual contamination?</li> <li>RAW is it feasible what I am proposing in the next paragraphs? (A bit lenghtly to put in a question)</li> </ol><br /> Essentially we are in a very very long campaign and I got the idea (based on the &quot;Memorial to the Merciless Ministers&quot; rite) to create an artificial P\u2019o as a weapon: the original ritual allowed to sacrifice a dot of P\u2019o to strenghten a request, here the plan would be to use Demon Jade as a medium, and get 10 different Kuei-Jin's with distinct P\u2019o natures to sacrifice a bit of each creating a fake Demon soul inside the jade, cleary a very evil semi or fully sentient weapon that is willing and capable of hurting the Yama Kings themselves during the conflicts to come. We expect this to be a sword or halberd, that either feeds on Demon Chi, or even generates its own, it would be terrific against (and inside of) Yomi Wan (We are nothing but ambicious).<br /> <br /> Of course there are many ways this could go horribly right, including but not limited to maiming our Kuei-Jin for no gain, altering their personalities, the new P\u2019o staying purely spiritual and becoming a new Demon in a create-your-own-villain scenario... We could end up building something that would grow up to be the Demon Emperor for all I know.<br /> <br /> But my character is a mage, hubris is not a personality flaw is an built-in feature. If it does not have world altering scope, I am not playing it correctly.<br /> <br /> I have Entropy, Mind, Spirit, Life, Prime, Life and Correspondence at 3 or higher","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":".  Added teh missing Spheres 11-26-2023, 10:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-26T18:50:29-08:00","id":1525989,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1525986-m20-and-kuei-jin#post1525986\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Greetings,<br /> <br /> Based in a long standing game, some doubts regarding Kindred of the East arise:<br /> Kuei-Jin can absorbe Quintessence when feeding, can mages use Yang, Yin and/or Demon Chi?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not as such, but that's probably good for a Resonance bonus, if that you're using that. Note that Demon Chi is pretty much Angst from Wraith, the power source of a Shadow and of Spectres, so it's going to give off vibes like Euthanatos Jhor.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If the answer to the previous question is YES, what levels of Prime and any other Sphere are needed?<br /> What levels and which Spheres are needed to dectect the P\u2019o Nature? </div> </div> </div>Spirit and Entropy, for whatever it is you use to pick up on a Shadow. In spite of claims to the contrary, the P'o of both Wraiths of the Jade Kingdom and of Gui Ren are pretty much just Shadows. If they were actually something different, they wouldn't use the same rules (specifically, the Hun would probably have all the Fetter stuff for both Shadow Fetters and regular ones, and P'o would have the Passions of both a Psyche and Shadow).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What levels and which Spheres are needed to alter/interact/modify the P\u2019o?<br /> In Yomi Wan, what levels and which Spheres are needed to protect against the spiritual contamination? </div> </div> </div>Prime and Spirit 5, or just don't tap into any energy flows while you're there. If you get caught, you don't have Spheres high enough to keep the ruler from fucking with you, unless you're on the order of Voormas, maybe. Otherwise, dealing with the denizens and trying to avoid them is either like being in the Dark Umbra or corrupt portions of the Middle Umbra (it has realms of both welding together).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> RAW is it feasible what I am proposing in the next paragraphs? (A bit lenghtly to put in a question)<br /> <br /> Essentially we are in a very very long campaign and I got the idea (based on the &quot;Memorial to the Merciless Ministers&quot; rite) to create an artificial P\u2019o as a weapon: the original ritual allowed to sacrifice a dot of P\u2019o to strenghten a request, here the plan would be to use Demon Jade as a medium, and get 10 different Kuei-Jin's with distinct P\u2019o natures to sacrifice a bit of each creating a fake Demon soul inside the jade, cleary a very evil semi or fully sentient weapon that is willing and capable of hurting the Yama Kings themselves during the conflicts to come. We expect this to be a sword or halberd, that either feeds on Demon Chi, or even generates its own, it would be terrific against (and inside of) Yomi Wan (We are nothing but ambicious). </div> </div> </div>That sounds like it would a very involved spiritual instrument, though by RAW I don't know if it would necessarily do anything spectacular unless your ST is letting you make Level 6+ talismans, spiritual instruments and such. Those tend to be highly ST-specific.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Of course there are many ways this could go horribly right, including but not limited to maiming our Kuei-Jin for no gain, altering their personalities, the new P\u2019o staying purely spiritual and becoming a new Demon in a create-your-own-villain scenario... We could end up building something that would grow up to be the Demon Emperor for all I know.<br /> <br /> But my character is a mage, hubris is not a personality flaw is an built-in feature. If it does not have world altering scope, I am not playing it correctly.<br /> <br /> I have Entropy, Mind, Spirit, Prime at 3 or higher </div> </div> </div>You can step into hell, I think, but you won't be doing much of anything else - the plan above is pretty far above your current pay grade. You'd also have to deal with the Goblin Jungle Near Realm to get there, which, for mages, is a chore on its own, though Mind might keep away the goblins. The aggressive plant life on the Scarlet Road, not so much. Alternately, you can try to sneak in under the nose of Yu Huang on the Ebon Road, but you might end up horribly mangling yourself slipping and falling repeatedly on the Ebon Path, which is apparently super-slick and near-frictionless.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-26T19:04:24-08:00","id":1525991,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar23_3.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"23\" data-vbnamecard=\"23\">Saur Ops Specialist</a> Thanks for the answer, can you please adjust your reply based on my update of the Spheres (I copied and pasted, but for some reason I did not paste Correspondence and Life when putting the message)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-26T23:34:36-08:00","id":1525994,"title":"","content":"You're going to have to clarify your Sphere levels, because saying that you have them all at 3 or higher leaves out a lot of important information.<br /> <br /> At any rate, you're still looking at a bit of a slog. You're not going to get lost along the Scarlet Road and end up in Malfeas thanks to Correspondence leading the way, most likely, but teleporting around might still be a bit much. Life might allow you to soak a bit more agg, but you should still avoid combat. Luckily, you seem to be able to conceal yourself from perception via Mind 3, but you'll want to stay away from the more powerful denizens even while concealed, because they might spot you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-27T07:38:31-08:00","id":1526006,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1525986-m20-and-kuei-jin?p=1525994#post1525994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're going to have to clarify your Sphere levels, because saying that you have them all at 3 or higher leaves out a lot of important information.<br /> <br /> At any rate, you're still looking at a bit of a slog. You're not going to get lost along the Scarlet Road and end up in Malfeas thanks to Correspondence leading the way, most likely, but teleporting around might still be a bit much. Life might allow you to soak a bit more agg, but you should still avoid combat. Luckily, you seem to be able to conceal yourself from perception via Mind 3, but you'll want to stay away from the more powerful denizens even while concealed, because they might spot you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, Entropy 5 (just bought last session), Life, Prime, Mind, Spirit, Correspondence at 3 (soon to buy the fourth dot of Prime or Spirit).<br /> <br /> I never asked, what is need to enter or leave Yomi without the Scarlet Road or Ebon Path, Spirit 5 and Correspondence 5? That seems relevant too and I just forgot it.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-27T09:25:28-08:00","id":1526010,"title":"","content":"If you go by either path, you only need to go into the Near Umbra, which I believe is still accessible with Spirit 3. Correspondence 3 could help teleport you along, but you'd be going in alone, which may or may not fit your mission parameters. You might also be able to use Correspondence and some other spheres to locate and open an existing gateway right into a hell tucked into a seemingly innocuous part of the landscape, but you'd have to contend with its guardians, which is either a hard fight or a masterful act of bribery, again depending on which hell.<br /> <br /> Apparently, M20 changed how you make spiritual objects; Spirit 4 technically is the &quot;bad&quot; way that gets cursed objects by forcing an unwilling spirit, while Prime 4 is used if the spirit is willing (your favorite Futurama joke here!).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}